   <div class="search-container" style="position: relative; width: 300px;">
     <input type="text" id="searchInput" placeholder="Search..." style="width: 100%; padding: 8px 40px 8px 12px; border: 1px solid #ccc; border-radius: 6px;">
     <button id="searchBtn" style="position: absolute; right: 8px; top: 50%; transform: translateY(-50%); background: none; border: none; cursor: pointer; padding: 4px;">
       <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
         <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M21 21l-6-6m2-5a7 7 0 11-14 0 7 7 0 0114 0z" />
       </svg>
     </button>
   </div>

   <script>
     const input = document.getElementById('searchInput');
     const btn = document.getElementById('searchBtn');

     btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
       const value = input.value.trim();
       console.log('Searching for:', value);
       // Call your function here
     });

     input.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
       if (e.key === 'Enter') btn.click();
     });
   </script>
   ```

6.  **Key Considerations & Best Practices**:
   - Wrap SVG in a `<button>` for accessibility and proper click handling
   - Use `type="button"` to prevent form submission
   - Add `aria-label` for screen readers
   - Handle Enter key for better UX
   - Prevent text overlap with right padding on input
   - Use relative/absolute positioning or flexbox
   - Provide both React and vanilla JS versions since framework isn't specified
   - Mention CSS options (Tailwind vs plain CSS)

