```html
<div class="search-wrapper" style="position: relative; width: 300px;">
  <input 
    type="text" 
    id="searchInput" 
    placeholder="Search..." 
    style="width: 100%; padding: 10px 40px 10px 12px; border: 1px solid #ccc; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 14px;"
  />
  <button 
    id="searchBtn" 
    type="button"
    style="position: absolute; right: 10px; top: 50%; transform: translateY(-50%); background: none; border: none; cursor: pointer; padding: 4px; color: #666;"
    aria-label="Search"
  >
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
      <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M21 21l-6-6m2-5a7 7 0 11-14 0 7 7 0 0114 0z" />
    </svg>
  </button>
</div>

<script>
  const input = document.getElementById('searchInput');
  const btn = document.getElementById('searchBtn');

  function handleSearch() {
    const value = input.value.trim();
    if (!value) return;

    // 👇 CALL YOUR FUNCTION HERE
    console.log('Searching for:', value);
    // yourCustomFunction(value);
  }

  btn.addEventListener('click', handleSearch);

  // Optional: trigger search on Enter key
  input.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
    if (e.key === 'Enter') handleSearch();
  });
</script>
```

### 🔑 Key Points:
1. **Wrap the SVG in a `<button>`** → Ensures proper click handling, keyboard accessibility, and screen reader support.
2. `type="button"` → Prevents accidental form submission if wrapped in a `<form>`.
3. **Right padding on input** (`pr-12` or `padding-right: 40px`) → Stops typed text from hiding behind the icon.
4. **Absolute positioning** → `right-3 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2` perfectly centers the icon vertically on the right side.
5. **Enter key support** → Added for better UX (users expect to press Enter to search).
6. **Trim & validate** → `trim()` removes accidental spaces, and the empty check prevents useless calls.

